{"title":"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems\">2014 AMC 12A #4</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems\">2014 AMC 10A #6</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_8_(Formula_Version)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 8 (Formula Version)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> cows give <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> gallons of milk in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> days. At this rate, how many gallons of milk will <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cows give in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3a59bb1293ee3f6dec19de4019a7178874219ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> days?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/b/c3be9b791407bb00c49aea7501d104ec91f3ff81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{bde}{ac}\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{ac}{bde}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{abde}{c}\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{bcde}{a}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{abc}{de}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"467\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We need to multiply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/f/8cf2f872fda858799ad4cbba2f4ca7ddeccd0112.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{d}{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"12\" height=\"37\" /> for the new cows and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/d/61d08b4711d8663836d8a7e013b66870b490d134.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{e}{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"10\" height=\"33\" /> for the new time, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/0/3f0fbffbb21dd6a320c5af98c9f02ae9721333bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b\\cdot \\frac{d}{a}\\cdot \\frac{e}{c}=\\frac{bde}{ac}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"112\" height=\"37\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/f/24fca6e9c48cc5b8088b3a1660a9eeacfe550505.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } \\frac{bde}{ac}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"78\" height=\"50\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We plug in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/a/55afdab16c8c49089c4d9ceeb8d3c8cf1f088be6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/6/626beed3a7eee094ce4b6cf79a49d81669f72d99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=3$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/3/c63e18205b2a13c9f8d283e834e0bb8d145ba305.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/6/0c69d1273beeeec5eb86e9cdd3bf326ddc98e0ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=5$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/b/61b88def425b07518734e46dbb0ef3659a60f7af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e=6$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />. Hence the question becomes \"2 cows give 3 gallons of milk in 4 days. How many gallons of milk do 5 cows give in 6 days?\"\n</p><p>If 2 cows give 3 gallons of milk in 4 days, then 2 cows give <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/1/e1150a17bf1b733cb666be84d920c71fc96bb3f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"11\" height=\"38\" /> gallons of milk in 1 day, so 1 cow gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/a/f8a9f70dda78b486829aaca7adb14e4973b19d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{4\\cdot2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"33\" height=\"38\" /> gallons in 1 day. This means that 5 cows give <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/9/469100e4351c7f3d239bf8e7c1c1d67a83783e3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5\\cdot3}{4\\cdot2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"33\" height=\"38\" /> gallons of milk in 1 day. Finally, we see that 5 cows give <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/d/31d1082c2b2b458be69ad2de3123ba689b3dfe7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5\\cdot3\\cdot6}{4\\cdot2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"59\" height=\"38\" /> gallons of milk in 6 days. Substituting our values for the variables, this becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/f/16f77c1a35eb7a6e4337a27c719c82294ab78a43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{dbe}{ac}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"28\" height=\"37\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/8/c9835ecbec2d5b06ca12663c9a7740533499c4b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{bde}{ac}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"76\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We see that the number of cows is inversely proportional to the number of days and directly proportional to the gallons of milk. So our constant is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/e/0be07c9d4f319dc48388ddb81ba38e87aa1c0e31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{ac}{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"19\" height=\"33\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be the answer to the question. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/6/816352c8eb723908f50c8fa0ac365bcb4a4b5c71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{de}{g}=\\dfrac{ac}{b}\\implies gac=bde\\implies g=\\dfrac{bde}{ac}\\implies\\boxed{ \\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{bde}{ac}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"432\" height=\"49\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The problem specifics \"rate,\" so it would be wise to first find the rate at which cows produce milk. We can find the rate of work/production by finding the gallons produced by a single cow in a single day. To do this, we divide the amount produced by the number of cows and number of days <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/3/bc326104c3a461a163a7429decb33c6d7b2f40d2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies\\text{rate}=\\dfrac{b}{ac}\\]\" width=\"111\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Now that we have the gallons produced by a single cow in a single day, we simply multiply that rate by the number of cows and the number of days <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/e/47e7878330df965d3a116bba82631d796ffa71e2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } \\dfrac{bde}{ac}}\\]\" width=\"115\" height=\"49\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> cows give <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> gallons of milk in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> days, that means that one cow will give <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/2/032cb0c5932179b6ceedd7baa2a7b33391437704.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{b}{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"12\" height=\"37\" /> gallons of milk in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> days. Also, we want to find the number of gallons of milk will <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cows give in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3a59bb1293ee3f6dec19de4019a7178874219ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> days, so in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/d/61d08b4711d8663836d8a7e013b66870b490d134.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{e}{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"10\" height=\"33\" /> days <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cows give <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/6/4e601902e89b9efb22938e65c0662c9fef1be520.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{bd}{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"19\" height=\"37\" /> gallons of milk. Multiplying with the formula <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1218dbfae7805ea5564ac7ee2a892d0a846653.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=rt$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/a/eaa3cd35dfe5da3f3924da78f737333011bf7e3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } \\dfrac{bde}{ac}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"78\" height=\"50\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the right formula, plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/1/b817c877bfd78e620a2d0c578989c7e4ee19d3bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=a$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/8/5e8132b76ee2f02d29775ad133e934f6b6c2a37a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e=c$\" width=\"40\" height=\"8\" /> should simplify to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, as if it doesn't, we'd essentially be saying \"<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> cows give <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> gallons of milk in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> days, but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> cows don't give <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> gallons of milk in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> days.\" The only one of the answer choices that simplifies like this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/e/35e8ea2d16518197b5113002b8c0c7da6c311a3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"41\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7\">Solution 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Call the rate at which a single cow produces milk <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. Using the given information we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/d/5bdab76b7050616af629549fbc6a3ba08918bec6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$rac=b$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" />, and we want to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/c/39cbf953875845fbf77fd873fa1ebef5d07d2369.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$rde$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />. We solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> in the first equation to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/c/17c17a5c7111627587d1ec8fe2038c2fd3e8f71d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=b \\cdot \\tfrac{1}{ac}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"73\" height=\"23\" />. Plugging in this value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> into the expression we want, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/9/8e9666725fa8867b879622cd826e8c759d0d47c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$rde=\\frac{bde}{ac}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"79\" height=\"37\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/e/35e8ea2d16518197b5113002b8c0c7da6c311a3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"41\" height=\"28\" />.'\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_8_.28Formula_Version.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_8_(Formula_Version)\">Solution 8 (Formula Version)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 8 (Formula Version)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can start by using the work formula <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/3/ff361e2d7defb0702a344be9334e713fb64769d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W = n \\cdot t \\cdot r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"98\" height=\"14\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/c/10cb764f88509fb1c8012366993fdbee98f31bc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" /> is the total work done (milk produced), <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is the number of workers (cows), <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> is the time (days), and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the rate of a single worker. (Note: I learned this special formula from the Aops book \"The Basics\" by Richard Rusczyk and I find it very useful and convenient when solving these problems)\n</p><p>From the first part of the problem, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> cows produce <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> gallons of milk in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> days. Substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/2/6427faa80403c771d1f0d7ac896dd1ec3208b051.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/b/01b53e066bb92f269c15aeae01b1edc05478a306.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W = b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/8/16890e9e38b08f608c53ed18db9c56d6024e0447.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t = c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" /> into our formula gives:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/4/ec4f469ff35a3247f8d5fc2788366f652c70a83a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = a \\cdot c \\cdot r \\implies r = \\frac{b}{ac}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"190\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>And just like that, we can continue by using the ways from the previous solutions to find the answer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/e/35e8ea2d16518197b5113002b8c0c7da6c311a3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"41\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User%EF%BC%9AIcosahedron0288#Created_Pages\" title=\"User：Icosahedron0288\">Icosahedron0288</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28CREATIVE_THINKING.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING)\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<pre><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/4THtSkiSGMg\">https://youtu.be/4THtSkiSGMg</a>\n</pre>\n<p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/OW4rHUTPgPA\">https://youtu.be/OW4rHUTPgPA</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid bla